 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Ciao LLM baseline scoring in ten Colab runs\n","\n","Choose a T4 GPU runtime. Set PARTITION_ID to a unique integer 0–9 on each account. Users are sorted and divided into ten contiguous balanced slices, so the slices are disjoint and cover all users. Start with batch size 8; lower it to 4 if CUDA runs out of memory.\n","\n","Load these four files into /content/data/Ciao/: train_data.csv, val_data.csv, test_data.csv, item_mapping.csv. CSV splits must be tab separated; mapping needs item and raw_item columns. No other preprocessed data files are needed. Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B weights download on first use."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["%pip -q install transformers accelerate pandas numpy"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\nimport json, hashlib\nimport pandas as pd\n\nPARTITION_ID = 0  # unique integer 0..9 on each account\nNUM_PARTITIONS = 10\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\nDATA_DIR = Path('/content/data/Ciao')\nOUT_DIR = Path('/content/llm_cache')\nMODEL_ID = 'Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B'\nCANDIDATE_POOL = 50\nHISTORY_LENGTH = 20\nassert 0 <= PARTITION_ID < NUM_PARTITIONS and BATCH_SIZE > 0\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Keep the baseline scorer unchanged\n","\n","Upload the repository file llm_baseline.py to /content (and install the project's requirements), then run the next cell. This uses its exact LocalHuggingFaceScorer, including prompt, generation, retries, parser, and neutral fallback. The scoring cell below reproduces build_llm_matching_scores candidate generation and cache settings, while restricting execution to this account's user partition."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["%pip -q install torch transformers accelerate numpy pandas"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '/content')\nfrom llm_baseline import LocalHuggingFaceScorer\nimport torch\nassert torch.cuda.is_available(), 'Enable T4 GPU runtime.'\nprint(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Read the same four processed inputs as the repository baseline.\ntrain_df=pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR/'train_data.csv',sep='\\t')\nval_df=pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR/'val_data.csv',sep='\\t')\ntest_df=pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR/'test_data.csv',sep='\\t')\nmapping=pd.read_csv(DATA_DIR/'item_mapping.csv')\nif not {'item','raw_item'}.issubset(mapping.columns): raise ValueError('item_mapping.csv requires item and raw_item')\nitem_names=dict(zip(mapping.item.astype(int),mapping.raw_item.astype(str)))\nnum_items=int(max(train_df.item.max(),val_df.item.max(),test_df.item.max()))+1\ncounts=train_df.item.value_counts().reindex(range(num_items),fill_value=0)\npopular_items=counts.sort_values(ascending=False).index.tolist()\nall_users=set(train_df.user.astype(int)); all_users.update(val_df.user.astype(int)); all_users.update(test_df.user.astype(int))\nuser_histories={int(u):g.sort_values('timestamp').item.astype(int).tolist() for u,g in train_df.groupby('user')}\nusers=sorted(all_users)\na=len(users)*PARTITION_ID//NUM_PARTITIONS; b=len(users)*(PARTITION_ID+1)//NUM_PARTITIONS; partition_users=users[a:b]\nprint(f'{len(users)} users total; partition {PARTITION_ID}: {len(partition_users)} users [{a}:{b})')\n# Same digest inputs/settings as llm_baseline.py, so all shards identify the same cache.\npool_size=max(int(CANDIDATE_POOL),1)\nsettings={'model_id':MODEL_ID,'candidate_pool':pool_size,'history_length':int(HISTORY_LENGTH),'num_items':int(num_items),'prompt_version':1}\nh=hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(settings,sort_keys=True).encode('utf-8'))\nh.update(pd.util.hash_pandas_object(train_df[['user','item','timestamp']],index=False).to_numpy().tobytes())\nh.update((DATA_DIR/'item_mapping.csv').read_bytes()); digest=h.hexdigest()\nOUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nout=OUT_DIR/f'llm_matching_scores_{digest}_part_{PARTITION_ID:02d}_of_10.json'\nscore_cache={int(u):{int(i):float(s) for i,s in v.items()} for u,v in json.loads(out.read_text()).items()} if out.exists() else {}\ncandidate_cache={}\nfor offset,user in enumerate(partition_users):\n print(f"Processing user {user} ({a+offset+1}/{len(users)})")\n history=user_histories.get(user,[]); positives=set(history); candidates=set(positives)\n for item in popular_items:\n  candidates.add(int(item))\n  if len(candidates)>=pool_size: break\n if positives and not any(item not in positives for item in candidates):\n  neg=next((int(i) for i in popular_items if int(i) not in positives),None)\n  if neg is not None: candidates.add(neg)\n candidate_cache[user]=sorted(candidates); score_cache.setdefault(user,{})\nscorer=None\nfor batch_start in range(0,len(partition_users),BATCH_SIZE):\n batch=partition_users[batch_start:batch_start+BATCH_SIZE]; requests=[]; request_users=[]\n for user in batch:\n  missing=[i for i in candidate_cache[user] if i not in score_cache[user]]\n  if missing:\n   history=user_histories.get(user,[])\n   profile='\\n'.join(item_names.get(i,f'Item {i}') for i in history[-HISTORY_LENGTH:]) or 'No prior item history.'\n   requests.append((profile,[(i,item_names.get(i,f'Item {i}')) for i in missing])); request_users.append(user)\n if requests:\n  if scorer is None: scorer=LocalHuggingFaceScorer(MODEL_ID,device='cuda')\n  results=scorer.score_batch(requests)\n  for user,scores in zip(request_users,results): score_cache[user].update(scores)\n out.write_text(json.dumps({str(u):{str(i):s for i,s in x.items()} for u,x in score_cache.items()}))\n print(f'Processed {min(batch_start+BATCH_SIZE,len(partition_users))}/{len(partition_users)} users')\nscore_cache={u:{i:score_cache[u][i] for i in ids} for u,ids in candidate_cache.items()}\nout.write_text(json.dumps({str(u):{str(i):s for i,s in x.items()} for u,x in score_cache.items()}))\nprint('Saved',len(score_cache),'users:',out)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Merge outputs\n","\n","Download one JSON file from each account. Check that the digest part of the filename matches and the partition suffixes are 00 through 09. Merge the top-level user objects into one JSON object (user_id → item_id → score). Save the result as .llm_cache/llm_matching_scores_<digest>.json to match the repository cache filename."]}
